      "match": "14px",
      "reason": "This selector matches no node in the component's current markup: it lives in a component the product does render, but nothing it renders is reached by it, so the declaration can never apply. Asserting a role over it would be asserting something unprovable. The distinction with a dead EXPORT is deliberate and decides the treatment: a whole component with no consumer is well formed and a fixture CAN mount it, so its role is demonstrable and it is migrated; a dead selector inside a live component is not.",
      "evidence": "SelectContent p: SettingsSelectUI/index.js:89-92 mete dentro de SelectContent un unico hijo, el Select compartido de Shared/UI, y Shared/UI/Select.jsx no renderiza ningun elemento <p> — su unica coincidencia de 'p>' en todo el archivo es el cierre de </SelectPrimitive.Popup>. El selector no alcanza a nada."
